e following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dec8cece-e79e-5652-812a-3c79c57417e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351409 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a diagonal matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 3=-24\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186352230 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186352230 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352230 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47f733f4-12f3-5c07-8f4b-304b44459b9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352356 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352356 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352356 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59881df0-2ac6-532e-8fb9-91b698aa746f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352433 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{10}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352433 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352433 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6136a078-6ec6-579a-809a-d2077533b6a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352607 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{111}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352607 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352607 #edb/ref 10