80 "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392527 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392527 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3737a2a5-a57d-571a-a651-f2cad4ee3049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400881 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400881 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140449" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400881 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400881 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186400881 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f772a19b-8ab2-5f26-9ef1-47231e01914d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400881 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186400882 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400882 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400882 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400882 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592